  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual advice as the recipient of moral instruction",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material as the intended recipient of the moral advice. The text explicitly uses 'you' ('you have the more girlfriends you have...') and 'your' ('your future'), directly addressing the viewer. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the person who must heed the advice, making the moralistic message feel personal and directed at them. The visual material (the man) is presented as the moral authority ('my brother') delivering this advice to 'you'.",
